<!-- Tailwind CSS vs Normal CSS: A Comparison
This document provides a comparison between Normal CSS and Tailwind CSS. It shows how common styling properties can be achieved using both approaches.
1. Text color, size, and weight
Normal CSS

.title {
  color: blue;
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
}

Tailwind CSS

<h1 class="text-blue-500 text-2xl font-bold">Hello</h1>

Explanation

In Tailwind CSS, we can achieve text color, size, and weight by using utility classes like 'text-blue-500', 'text-2xl', and 'font-bold'. 
Normal CSS requires explicit styling using the 'color', 'font-size', and 'font-weight' properties.

